{"id":"fresh_01","grade":1,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A class packs 4 bags with 6 oranges in each bag. How many oranges are packed altogether?","exact_reference_answer":"24 oranges","checker":"exact_numeric_with_unit","oracle":{"value":"24","unit":"oranges"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Multiply 4 equal groups of 6.","State 24 oranges."],"must_not_require":["A particular multiplication strategy or extra explanation."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_02","grade":1,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"Mina sees 3 red kites and 5 blue kites at the park. How many kites does she see?","exact_reference_answer":"8 kites","checker":"exact_numeric_with_unit","oracle":{"value":"8","unit":"kites"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Combine 3 and 5.","State 8 kites."],"must_not_require":["An unrequested drawing or explanation."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_03","grade":1,"mode":"hint_no_answer","userproblem":"There are 4 rows of chairs with 3 chairs in every row. How could you find the total number of chairs?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"no_final_answer","oracle":{"behavior":"Give a first-step hint about equal groups or repeated addition; do not compute or state the total."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Suggest counting equal groups or adding 3 four times."],"must_not_do":["State the final total or an equivalent completed calculation."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_04","grade":1,"mode":"missing_or_contradictory_info","userproblem":"A jar had 4 marbles. Leo put 7 more marbles into it. How many marbles are left in the jar?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"identify_question_mismatch","oracle":{"behavior":"Point out that no marbles were said to be removed; ask whether the intended question is how many there are now."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Use only the stated facts.","Identify the mismatch between adding marbles and asking how many are left."],"must_not_do":["Invent a removal event."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_05","grade":2,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A library puts 8 storybooks on each of 3 display shelves. How many storybooks are on those shelves?","exact_reference_answer":"24 storybooks","checker":"exact_numeric_with_unit","oracle":{"value":"24","unit":"storybooks"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Find 3 groups of 8.","State 24 storybooks."],"must_not_require":["A particular multiplication algorithm."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_06","grade":2,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A school collected 37 cans on Monday and 19 on Tuesday. How many cans did it collect over the two days?","exact_reference_answer":"56 cans","checker":"exact_numeric_with_unit","oracle":{"value":"56","unit":"cans"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Add the two daily counts.","State 56 cans."],"must_not_require":["An unrequested explanation of addition."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_07","grade":2,"mode":"hint_no_answer","userproblem":"A rectangular garden is 5 meters long and 2 meters wide. What is its perimeter?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"no_final_answer","oracle":{"behavior":"Hint to add all four side lengths or use two lengths plus two widths; do not calculate the perimeter."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Direct attention to the four boundary sides and their lengths."],"must_not_do":["State the perimeter or complete its calculation."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_08","grade":2,"mode":"student_error","userproblem":"I counted 34 beads and then got 28 more. My work is 4 + 8 = 12, write 2 and carry 1; then 3 + 2 + 1 = 5, so the answer is 52 beads. Can you help me check my work?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"feedback_grounded_in_student_work","oracle":{"behavior":"Acknowledge the shown carrying steps and identify that the tens column must include the carried ten; give a supportive correction grounded in the written work."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Refer to the student's written carry from 4+8.","Explain the specific place-value correction supportively."],"must_not_do":["Attribute an error not present in the supplied work."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_09","grade":3,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A team labels 45 water bottles and puts them equally into 6 crates. How many full crates can they make, and how many bottles remain?","exact_reference_answer":"7 full crates, 3 bottles remain","checker":"exact_quotient_remainder","oracle":{"quotient":"7","remainder":"3","unit":"bottles"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Report 7 full crates.","Report 3 bottles remaining."],"must_not_require":["A particular division notation."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_10","grade":3,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A recipe uses 3/4 cup of oats per batch. How many cups of oats are needed for 4 batches?","exact_reference_answer":"3 cups","checker":"exact_fraction","oracle":{"value":"3","unit":"cups"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Multiply 3/4 cup by 4 batches.","State 3 cups."],"must_not_require":["Unrequested recipe advice."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_11","grade":3,"mode":"hint_no_answer","userproblem":"A ribbon is 3/5 meter long. What fraction of a meter would 2 such ribbons measure together?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"no_final_answer","oracle":{"behavior":"Suggest combining two equal fractional lengths, for example by adding 3/5 twice; do not simplify or state the result."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Point to adding two copies of the given fraction."],"must_not_do":["State the resulting fraction or equivalent final length."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_12","grade":3,"mode":"missing_or_contradictory_info","userproblem":"A bottle is labeled as holding 750 mL, but the note says it currently contains 900 mL. What fraction of the bottle's capacity is filled?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"flag_inconsistent_capacity","oracle":{"behavior":"Explain that the stated contents exceed the stated capacity, so the fraction-full question conflicts with the given information; ask which measurement should be corrected."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Compare contents with stated capacity.","State that the given quantities conflict for a filled bottle."],"must_not_do":["Silently change either measurement."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_13","grade":4,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A school walk is 180 kilometers and takes 3 hours at a steady speed. What is the speed in kilometers per hour?","exact_reference_answer":"60 kilometers per hour","checker":"exact_rate","oracle":{"value":"60","unit":"kilometers per hour"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Divide distance by time.","State 60 kilometers per hour."],"must_not_require":["A particular unit-conversion discussion."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_14","grade":4,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A club has 40 members. Three-fifths of them signed up for the nature walk. How many members signed up?","exact_reference_answer":"24 members","checker":"exact_fraction_of_quantity","oracle":{"value":"24","unit":"members"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Find three-fifths of 40.","State 24 members."],"must_not_require":["Extra claims about the remaining members."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_15","grade":4,"mode":"hint_no_answer","userproblem":"A triangular flag has a base of 10 centimeters and a perpendicular height of 6 centimeters. How could you find its area?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"no_final_answer","oracle":{"behavior":"Hint that triangle area uses one-half times base times perpendicular height; do not evaluate it."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Identify the triangle area relationship using the given base and height."],"must_not_do":["Calculate or state the area."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_16","grade":4,"mode":"student_error","userproblem":"I multiplied 2.5 by 4 like this: 25 × 4 = 100, then I put the decimal point after one digit and wrote 1.0. Is my answer right?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"feedback_grounded_in_student_work","oracle":{"behavior":"Explain that the whole-number product is 100 in hundredths after scaling by ten, so placing the decimal for 2.5 times 4 gives 10; address the student's stated decimal placement gently."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Refer to the student's 25 × 4 work and decimal placement.","Correct the placement and explain the scale briefly."],"must_not_do":["Claim the multiplication 25 × 4 is itself wrong."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_17","grade":5,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"Two friends share 45 stickers in the ratio 2:3. How many stickers does the friend represented by the 2 receive?","exact_reference_answer":"18 stickers","checker":"exact_ratio_share","oracle":{"value":"18","unit":"stickers"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Use 5 equal ratio parts in total.","State that the 2-part share is 18 stickers."],"must_not_require":["A diagram or a particular ratio method."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_18","grade":5,"mode":"answer","userproblem":"A storage box is 12 centimeters long, 5 centimeters wide, and 4 centimeters high. What is its volume?","exact_reference_answer":"240 cubic centimeters","checker":"exact_volume","oracle":{"value":"240","unit":"cubic centimeters"},"rubric":{"must_do":["Multiply the three dimensions.","State 240 cubic centimeters."],"must_not_require":["Surface area or a discussion of material."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_19","grade":5,"mode":"hint_no_answer","userproblem":"A jacket costs 80 dollars before a 15% discount. How could you work out the discount amount?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"no_final_answer","oracle":{"behavior":"Suggest finding 15 percent of 80, perhaps by using 10 percent and 5 percent; do not give the discount amount or sale price."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Offer a method to find 15% of $80."],"must_not_do":["State the discount amount or sale price."]},"not_training_data":true}
{"id":"fresh_20","grade":5,"mode":"missing_or_contradictory_info","userproblem":"A rectangular floor is said to have area 30 square meters and width 5 meters. The note also says its length is 4 meters. Which length and width should be used to order edging for the floor?","exact_reference_answer":null,"checker":"flag_inconsistent_rectangle_measurements","oracle":{"behavior":"Point out that 5 by 4 gives area 20 square meters, not the stated 30; ask which measurement is correct before choosing dimensions."},"rubric":{"must_do":["Identify the conflict between 30 square meters and 5 by 4 meters.","Ask for clarification rather than choosing one source."],"must_not_do":["Silently override the area or one dimension."]},"not_training_data":true}
